<% layout("/layouts/boilerplate") -%>

<main
  class="container my-5"
  style="max-width: 1040px; font-family: sans-serif; color: #222222"
>
  <nav aria-label="breadcrumb" class="mb-4">
    <ol
      class="breadcrumb"
      style="font-size: 14px; background: none; padding: 0"
    >
      <li class="breadcrumb-item">
        <a href="#" class="text-secondary text-decoration-none">Home</a>
      </li>
      <li class="breadcrumb-item">
        <a href="#" class="text-secondary text-decoration-none">All topics</a>
      </li>
      <li class="breadcrumb-item">
        <a href="#" class="text-secondary text-decoration-none">Legal Terms</a>
      </li>
      <li class="breadcrumb-item">
        <a href="#" class="text-secondary text-decoration-none"
          >Terms of Service</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="breadcrumb-item active text-dark" aria-current="page">
        Terms of Service
      </li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <div class="row g-5">
    <div class="col-md-8">
      <span class="text-muted small d-block mb-1">Legal terms</span>
      <h1 class="fw-bold mb-4" style="font-size: 2.3rem">Terms of Service</h1>

      <p class="text-muted mb-4" style="font-size: 14px">
        Last updated: April 17, 2026
      </p>

      <p class="fs-5 mb-4" style="line-height: 1.6; color: #484848">
        These Terms of Service constitute a legally binding agreement
        ("Agreement") between you and Airbnb governing your access to and use of
        the Airbnb website, application, and platform services.
      </p>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3" style="font-size: 1.4rem">1. Guest Terms</h3>
        <p style="line-height: 1.6; color: #484848">
          When you book a Listing, you are agreeing to enter into a contract
          directly with the Host. You are responsible for reading and
          understanding all rules, standards, policies, and requirements
          identified in the Listing or during checkout before completing your
          reservation.
        </p>
        <ul class="lh-lg" style="padding-left: 20px; color: #222222">
          <li>
            <strong>Cancellations and Refunds:</strong> If you cancel a
            reservation, the amount refunded is determined exclusively by the
            cancellation policy applying to that booking.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Booking Modifications:</strong> Guests and Hosts are
            responsible for any modifications to a booking that they agree to
            via the Airbnb Platform.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your Responsibilities:</strong> You are responsible for your
            own acts and omissions and are also responsible for the acts of any
            individual you invite to join your reservation.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3" style="font-size: 1.4rem">2. Host Terms</h3>
        <p style="line-height: 1.6; color: #484848">
          As a Host, Airbnb makes available the platform for you to offer
          accommodations, experiences, or other services to our global member
          base.
        </p>
        <ul class="lh-lg" style="padding-left: 20px; color: #222222">
          <li>
            <strong>Contracting with Guests:</strong> When you accept a booking
            request or receive a booking confirmation, you enter a contract
            directly with the Guest. You are bound to deliver your service under
            the terms specified in your listing.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Independence of Hosts:</strong> Your relationship with
            Airbnb is that of an independent individual or entity, and not an
            employee, agent, joint venturer, or partner.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3" style="font-size: 1.4rem">
          3. Content Policy and Licensing
        </h3>
        <p style="line-height: 1.6; color: #484848">
          Parts of the Airbnb Platform enable you to provide feedback, text,
          photos, reviews, and other media ("Content"). By uploading content,
          you grant Airbnb a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free,
          sub-licensable, and transferable license to access, store, use,
          distribute, publish, and translate your text and media for the
          operational term of platform features.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3" style="font-size: 1.4rem">
          4. Member Violations and Account Suspensions
        </h3>
        <p style="line-height: 1.6; color: #484848">
          To ensure a secure environment, safety violations, terms avoidance,
          off-platform behavior, or repeated negative reviews can result in
          strict operational actions against your profile. Airbnb reserves the
          right to:
        </p>
        <ul class="lh-lg" style="padding-left: 20px; color: #222222">
          <li>
            Suspend or limit your access to or use of the Airbnb platform
            features.
          </li>
          <li>
            Remove, disable, or restrict the visibility of active Listings or
            user Reviews.
          </li>
          <li>
            Cancel pending or confirmed reservations without system penalty to
            the affected counterparty.
          </li>
          <li>
            Revoke special operational indicators like host Superhost badges.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <hr class="my-5" style="border-top: 1px solid #dddddd" />

      <h2 class="fw-bold mb-4" style="font-size: 1.6rem">Related articles</h2>

      <div class="mb-4">
        <span class="text-muted small d-block mb-1">Legal terms</span>
        <a
          href="#"
          class="text-dark fw-bold d-block text-decoration-underline mb-1"
          >Additional Legal Terms</a
        >
        <p class="text-secondary small">
          Review properties regarding mandatory country-specific provisions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-4">
        <span class="text-muted small d-block mb-1">Legal terms</span>
        <a
          href="#"
          class="text-dark fw-bold d-block text-decoration-underline mb-1"
          >Service Fees Policy</a
        >
        <p class="text-secondary small">
          This document breaks down how fees are split between guest checkouts
          and host payouts.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-4">
        <span class="text-muted small d-block mb-1">Community policy</span>
        <a
          href="#"
          class="text-dark fw-bold d-block text-decoration-underline mb-1"
          >Major Disruptive Events Policy</a
        >
        <p class="text-secondary small" style="max-width: 550px">
          Find details regarding cancellations and protections when major
          unforeseen events break out post-booking.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

<div class="position-fixed bottom-0 end-0 m-4">
  <button
    class="btn btn-dark rounded-pill px-3 py-2 fw-bold"
    style="font-size: 14px"
  >
    ↑ Back to top
  </button>
</div>
